1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,184
Small law firms lose clients in the intake form.

2
00:00:03,234 --> 00:00:06,963
Older clients, people at work, anyone reading a second language.

3
00:00:07,013 --> 00:00:08,203
They don't finish it.

4
00:00:08,253 --> 00:00:12,041
So we made the form four fields, and let the phone do the intake.

5
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:14,219
This is Nota Intake.

6
00:00:14,269 --> 00:00:22,422
The client picks their language, leaves a name and number, and the interview language follows the phone number, straight from CALL-E's region table.

7
00:00:22,472 --> 00:00:24,917
A US number gets English or Bahasa Indonesia.

8
00:00:24,967 --> 00:00:26,580
A Mexican number gets Spanish.

9
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:29,573
The page tells you honestly what your number supports.

10
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:33,868
Submit, and within a minute CALL-E calls the client back.

11
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:44,420
This is a real call from our tests, reconstructed from the CALL-E transcript with a synthetic voice, since CALL-E doesn't return audio.

12
00:00:44,470 --> 00:00:56,020
It confirms the name, states that this is intake and not legal advice, then works through the matter, the other party for the conflict check, deadlines, urgency, best time to reach them, and consent.

13
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:52,162
Thirty seconds after the call, the paralegal has this.

14
00:01:52,212 --> 00:02:01,075
Matter type, a summary, the opposing party's name for the conflict check, urgency, consent, and the full transcript, with CALL-E's confidence score.

15
00:02:01,125 --> 00:02:02,761
Completion confidence: high.

16
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:04,329
Same number, different language.

17
00:02:04,379 --> 00:02:08,367
This is the Bahasa Indonesia call, also real, also on a US line.

18
00:02:08,417 --> 00:02:12,469
Adding a language is one row in a JSON file and one script block.

19
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:21,270
One click schedules a consultation reminder call, in the client's language, with its own result schema: confirmed, or a reschedule request.

20
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:22,995
One limit, stated plainly.

21
00:02:23,045 --> 00:02:25,834
CALL-E does not carry Spanish on US lines yet.

22
00:02:25,884 --> 00:02:29,290
We tried the locale, the task text, and the MCP planner.

23
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:31,389
All three declined before dialing.

24
00:02:31,439 --> 00:02:33,858
The Spanish script is written and wired;

25
00:02:33,908 --> 00:02:38,178
until it's enabled, those callers go to a human, and the form says so.

26
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:39,999
No servers.

27
00:02:40,049 --> 00:02:47,284
Cloudflare Pages, a few Functions, KV, and the CALL-E API with result schemas, webhooks, and idempotency keys.

28
00:02:47,334 --> 00:02:50,066
Repo and live link are in the description.

29
00:02:50,116 --> 00:02:51,391
This is Nota Intake.
